  "id": "pittsburgh",
  "intro": "Pittsburgh is the hardest VHF terrain of any city on this site. Three rivers cut deep valleys through a plateau, the neighbourhoods sit on ridges between them, and a handheld in one valley cannot hear a handheld in the next. This makes it genuinely interesting: coverage is a puzzle, repeater siting is an art, and a walk up Mount Washington changes everything you can hear. The rivers themselves are working commercial waterways with locks and coal tows, and the airport sits out on the plateau where the terrain finally flattens.",
  "introz": "匹兹堡是本站所有城市中 VHF 地形最难的一个。三条河在台地上切出深谷，各个街区坐落在谷间的山脊上，一条谷里的手台听不见隔壁谷里的手台。这反而让它格外有意思：覆盖是一道谜题，中继选址是一门手艺，而走上华盛顿山会彻底改变你能听到的内容。这些河本身是繁忙的商业水道，有船闸和运煤顶推船；机场则在台地外围地形终于变平的地方。",
